The '''2025 Ballon d'Or''' ({{lit|'''2025 Golden Ball'''}}) was the 69th annual ceremony of the [[Ballon d'Or]], presented by ''[[France Football]]'', recognising the best footballers in the world in the 2024–25 season. For the fourth time in the history of the award, it was awarded based on the results of the season instead of the calendar year. This was the period from 1 August 2024 to 13 July 2025 ([[2025 FIFA Club World Cup final|final]] of the [[2025 FIFA Club World Cup]]) for the men's award, and to 2 August 2025 ([[2025 Copa América Femenina final|final]] of the [[2025 Copa América Femenina]]) for the women's award. The ceremony took place on 22 September 2025, with the nominees having been announced on 7 August 2025.<ref name="UEFA">{{cite news |title=2025 Ballon d'Or ceremony date, venue and awards announced |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0299-1dcb47a46ca9-683cdc08a032-1000--2025-ballon-d-or-ceremony-date-venue-and-awards-announced/ |publisher=[[UEFA]] |access-date=24 May 2025 |date=19 May 2025 |archive-date=24 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250524102215/https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0299-1dcb47a46ca9-683cdc08a032-1000--2025-ballon-d-or-ceremony-date-venue-and-awards-announced/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="SportsIllustrated">{{cite magazine |last=Mallow |first=Max |date=19 May 2025 |title=Ballon d'Or 2025 Ceremony Date, Location Announced |url=https://www.si.com/soccer/ballon-dor-2025-ceremony-date-location-announced |access-date=24 May 2025 |magazine=[[Sports Illustrated]] |issn=0038-822X |archive-date=24 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250524102103/https://www.si.com/soccer/ballon-dor-2025-ceremony-date-location-announced |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2025/sep/22/ousmane-dembele-aitana-bonmati-ballon-dor-awards-football|title=Ousmane Dembélé and Aitana ¬Bonmatí land Ballon d'Or awards as England duo honoured|date=22 September 2025|work=Guardian|accessdate=23 September 2025}}</ref>

